1	line	Eadgar	Oh, it's you. Have you got me a parrot yet?
1	line	Parrot	Raaawk! Polly wanna cracker!
1	line	Player	Here it is! Now are you going to explain your plan?
1	line	Eadgar	Yes, yes, of course. It's quite ingenious really!
1	line	Eadgar	What we need is something that looks like a human, sounds like a human, smells like a human and tastes like a human.
1	line	Player	How are we going to make it look like a human?
1	line	Eadgar	We'll just make a scarecrow. We'll need logs, and 10 sheaves of wheat for stuffing.
1	line	Player	How are we going to make it sound like a human?
1	line	Eadgar	That's what the parrot's for, of course.
1	line	Parrot	Who's a pretty boy then?
1	line	Eadgar	Although the trolls might get suspicious if it doesn't say what they expect a human to say...
1	line	Eadgar	You should hide it for a while somewhere it can pick up some more appropriate catchphrases.
1	line	Player	How are we going to make it smell like a human?
1	line	Eadgar	Well, we'll need to dress it up anyway; if we use dirty clothes it'll smell human to the trolls.
1	line	Eadgar	I'm a man of few clothes myself, so you might want to ask old Sanfew about that one.
1	line	Player	And how are we going to make it taste like a human?
1	line	Eadgar	That's easy, we'll just stuff it with a few chickens. Everything tastes like chicken! Five raw chickens should be enough.
1	line	Eadgar	That's the plan. Anything else I can do for you?
